{"raw": {"https://onu.wd501.myworkdayjobs.com/ONU/job/Ohio-Northern-University/Adjunct-Instructor-of-Pharmacy_JR100323": {"title": "Adjunct Instructor of Pharmacy", "description": "Posted: 2026-10-13\nPart time\n\nCareer Opportunities at Ohio Northern University Job Summary: The Raabe College of Pharmacy at Ohio Northern University welcomes applicants for a part-time, adjunct faculty position. Candidates with backgrounds in all areas of Pharmacy will be considered. We seek individuals who are passionate about teaching and invested in student success. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue in order to fill positions as needed each fall and each spring semester. Candidates with a PharmD degree and experience teaching Pharmacy at the university level are encouraged to apply. Please ensure that your CV includes the names and contact information (phone + email) for 3 professional references. Job Description : Successful candidates will serve as instructors of record for lecture courses, laboratories, or other courses as assigned. Typical assignments include one or two courses each semester. Questions concerning the position should be directed to the chair of the Department of Pharmacy Practice, Dr. Brittany Bates, at b-bates.1@onu.edu . Your next professional chapter begins here! ONU is an equal employment opportunity employer. Accordingly, no person shall be discriminated against on the basis of race, color, sex, gender identity, transgender status, religion, national origin, age, disability, sexual orientation, marital status, military or veteran status, genetic information or any other category protected by federal, state, or local law. This policy applies to all areas of employment including recruitment, hiring, training and development, promotion, transfer, compensation, benefits, discipline, separation and other terms, condition and privileges of employment."}, "https://onu.wd501.myworkdayjobs.com/ONU/job/Ohio-Northern-University/Visiting-Assistant-Professor-Instructor-of-Statistics_JR100302": {"title": "Visiting Assistant Professor/Instructor of Statistics", "description": "Posted: 2026-10-12\nFull time\n\nCareer Opportunities at Ohio Northern University Job Summary: The Department of Statistics & Applied Technology in the Getty College of Arts & Sciences at Ohio Northern University welcomes applicants for a visiting assistant professor position in statistics for the spring 2027 semester. We seek a talented individual who is invested in student success and passionate about teaching introductory teaching foundational introductory courses to students in a diverse group of programs across four colleges (Arts & Sciences, Business, Engineering, and Pharmacy). If you desire to make a difference in the lives of undergraduate students, we invite you to apply for a visiting position to begin January 19, 2027. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. A master\u2019s degree in Statistics or a related discipline is required. Candidates with doctoral degrees or experience teaching Statistics at the university level are encouraged to apply. Appointment rank will be commensurate with degree. The successful candidate will demonstrate a commitment to inclusive pedagogical strategies that engage today\u2019s students in both the classroom, as well as strong interpersonal skills. Job Description : The successful candidate will teach introductory statistics courses for a broad range of majors, including business, biology, criminal justice, exercise physiology, and nursing majors. Ohio Northern University faculty teach 23-25 credit hours per year. Additional responsibilities include advising undergraduate students and service. Please submit the following documents to ensure your application is complete: Cover letter. CV that includes the names and contact information (phone + email) for 3 professional references. Statement of teaching philosophy - please discuss how you would or have supported a classroom of students with a broad cross-section of differing levels of academic preparation. Unofficial transcripts for your undergraduate and graduate degrees. Questions concerning the position should be directed to the Director of the School for Mathematical & Physical Sciences, Dr. Tevye Celius, at t-celius@onu.edu. The Getty College of Arts & Sciences is proud to focus exclusively on undergraduate education. We place a premium on faculty who provide close mentoring through small classrooms and experiential learning. Our students share a passion for learning that goes beyond the classroom across 35 nationally acclaimed and accredited degree programs. A&S students are fueled by a commitment to make a difference in their local and global communities. The College of Arts & Sciences has an impressive record of professional accomplishments by our alumni. Ohio Northern University ranks in the top 100 private universities in the U.S. ONU is ranked #1 in the state of Ohio for Best Value and #31 in the U.S. for Best Value by U.S. News & World Report . Located in Ada, Ohio, the University\u2019s rural setting provides a rhythm of life that is peaceful and unhurried. The natural beauty of campus and the friendliness of the village and university communities offer an ideal setting for the pursuit of knowledge and genuine relationships. Additional information about Ohio Northern University is available at http://www.onu.edu Your next professional chapter begins here! ONU is an equal employment opportunity employer. Accordingly, no person shall be discriminated against on the basis of race, color, sex, gender identity, transgender status, religion, national origin, age, disability, sexual orientation, marital status, military or veteran status, genetic information or any other category protected by federal, state, or local law. This policy applies to all areas of employment including recruitment, hiring, training and development, promotion, transfer, compensation, benefits, discipline, separation and other terms, condition and privileges of employment."}, "https://onu.wd501.myworkdayjobs.com/ONU/job/Ohio-Northern-University/Assistant-Professor-of-Statistics_JR100306": {"title": "Assistant Professor of Statistics", "description": "Posted: 2026-10-12\nFull time\n\nCareer Opportunities at Ohio Northern University Job Summary: The Department of Statistics & Applied Technology in the Getty College of Arts & Sciences at Ohio Northern University welcomes applicants for a tenure-track, assistant professor position in Statistics. We seek a talented individual who is (1) passionate about teaching foundational introductory courses to students in a diverse group of programs across four colleges (Arts & Sciences, Business, Engineering, and Pharmacy), (2) excited to teach upper-division courses geared toward majors in Statistics and minors in Applied Statistics and Data Analytics, (3) committed to scholarship involving undergraduates, and (4) deeply invested in student success. If you desire to make a difference in the lives of undergraduate students, we invite you to apply for a tenure-track faculty position to begin August 17, 2027. Review of applications will begin October 15, 2026 and continue until the position is filled. A terminal degree in Statistics, Biostatistics, Data Science, Data Analytics, or a closely related field is required. ABD candidates will be considered if all degree requirements are completed before September 1, 2027. The successful candidate will demonstrate strong interpersonal skills, as well as the interest and ability to mentor students both inside and outside the classroom. Candidates with experience teaching undergraduate statistics courses and involvement in undergraduate research are encouraged to apply. Job Description : The successful candidate will teach a variety of undergraduate Statistics courses. Ohio Northern faculty in the College of Arts & Sciences teach 23-25 credit hours per year. Additional responsibilities include advising undergraduate students, scholarship and mentoring undergraduate research, and sharing university, college, and department service responsibilities. Please submit the following documents to ensure your application is complete: Cover letter. CV that includes the names and contact information (phone + email) for 3 professional references. Statement of teaching philosophy - please discuss how you would or have supported a classroom of students with a broad cross-section of differing levels of academic preparation. Statement of proposed scholarship that involves undergraduates. Unofficial transcripts for your undergraduate and graduate degrees. Questions concerning the position should be directed to Dr. Ryan Rahrig, Search Committee Chair at r-rahrig@onu.edu. The Getty College of Arts & Sciences is proud to focus exclusively on undergraduate education. We place a premium on faculty who provide close mentoring through small classrooms and experiential learning. Our students share a passion for learning that goes beyond the classroom across 35 nationally acclaimed and accredited degree programs. A&S students are fueled by a commitment to make a difference in their local and global communities. The College of Arts & Sciences has an impressive record of professional accomplishments by our alumni. Ohio Northern University ranks in the top 100 private universities in the U.S. ONU is ranked #1 in the state of Ohio for Best Value and #31 in the U.S. for Best Value by U.S. News & World Report . Located in Ada, Ohio, the University\u2019s rural setting provides a rhythm of life that is peaceful and unhurried. The natural beauty of campus and the friendliness of the village and university communities offer an ideal setting for the pursuit of knowledge and genuine relationships. Additional information about Ohio Northern University is available at http://www.onu.edu . Your next professional chapter begins here! ONU is an equal employment opportunity employer. Accordingly, no person shall be discriminated against on the basis of race, color, sex, gender identity, transgender status, religion, national origin, age, disability, sexual orientation, marital status, military or veteran status, genetic information or any other category protected by federal, state, or local law. This policy applies to all areas of employment including recruitment, hiring, training and development, promotion, transfer, compensation, benefits, discipline, separation and other terms, condition and privileges of employment."}, "https://onu.wd501.myworkdayjobs.com/ONU/job/Ohio-Northern-University/Associate-Professor-of-Technology_JR100305": {"title": "Assistant or Associate Professor of Construction Management", "description": "Posted: 2026-10-12\nFull time\n\nCareer Opportunities at Ohio Northern University Job Summary: The Department of Statistics & Applied Technology in the Getty College of Arts & Sciences at Ohio Northern University welcomes applicants for a tenure-track, assistant or associate professor position in Construction Management. Rank commensurate with experience. We seek a talented individual who is (1) passionate about teaching both lower-division and upper-division undergraduate courses in Construction Management, (2) committed to scholarship, and (3) invested in student success. If you desire to make a difference in the lives of undergraduate students, we invite you to apply for a tenure-track faculty position to begin either January 19, 2027 or August 17, 2027. Review of applications will begin October 15, 2026 and continue until the position is filled. A terminal degree in Construction Management, Construction Engineering, Engineering Technologies, Civil Engineering, or a closely related field is required. ABD candidates will be considered if all degree requirements are completed before September 1, 2027. Candidates with experience teaching undergraduate construction management courses or industry experience are encouraged to apply. Job Description : The successful candidate will teach a variety of undergraduate courses such as Introduction to CAD, Fluid and Mechanical Systems, Design, Estimating, Scheduling, Project Controls, and Project Management/Administration. Ohio Northern faculty in the College of Arts & Sciences teach 23-25 credit hours per year. Additional responsibilities include scholarship and service, including advising undergraduate students and student organizations (e.g., competition coaching) and maintaining industry relationships. Please submit the following documents to ensure your application is complete: Cover letter. CV that includes the names and contact information (phone + email) for 3 professional references. Statement of teaching philosophy - please discuss how you would or have supported a classroom of students with a broad cross-section of differing levels of academic preparation. Statement of proposed research suitable for a primarily undergraduate institution. Unofficial transcripts for your undergraduate and graduate degrees. Questions concerning the position should be directed to the Search Committee Chair at t-celius@onu.edu The Getty College of Arts & Sciences is proud to focus exclusively on undergraduate education. We place a premium on faculty who provide close mentoring through small classrooms and experiential learning. Our students share a passion for learning that goes beyond the classroom across 35 nationally acclaimed and accredited degree programs. A&S students are fueled by a commitment to make a difference in their local and global communities. The College of Arts & Sciences has an impressive record of professional accomplishments by our alumni. Ohio Northern University ranks in the top 100 private universities in the U.S. ONU is ranked #1 in the state of Ohio for Best Value and #31 in the U.S. for Best Value by U.S. News & World Report . Located in Ada, Ohio, the University\u2019s rural setting provides a rhythm of life that is peaceful and unhurried. The natural beauty of campus and the friendliness of the village and university communities offer an ideal setting for the pursuit of knowledge and genuine relationships. Additional information about Ohio Northern University is available at http://www.onu.edu . Your next professional chapter begins here! ONU is an equal employment opportunity employer. Accordingly, no person shall be discriminated against on the basis of race, color, sex, gender identity, transgender status, religion, national origin, age, disability, sexual orientation, marital status, military or veteran status, genetic information or any other category protected by federal, state, or local law. This policy applies to all areas of employment including recruitment, hiring, training and development, promotion, transfer, compensation, benefits, discipline, separation and other terms, condition and privileges of employment."}, "https://onu.wd501.myworkdayjobs.com/ONU/job/Ohio-Northern-University/Assistant-Professor-of-Communication_JR100304": {"title": "Assistant Professor of Communication", "description": "Posted: 2026-10-12\nFull time\n\nCareer Opportunities at Ohio Northern University Job Summary: The Department of Art & Communication in the Getty College of Arts & Sciences at Ohio Northern University welcomes applicants for a tenure-track, assistant professor position in Communication, with a specialization in Interpersonal and/or Organizational Communication. We seek a talented individual who is (1) passionate about teaching that bridges theoretical foundations in Communication with real-world practice, (2) committed to interdisciplinary scholarship that involves undergraduates, and (3) invested in student success. If you desire to make a difference in the lives of students, we invite you to apply for a tenure-track faculty position to begin August 17, 2027. Review of applications will begin October 22, 2026 and continue until the position is filled. A Ph.D. in Communication Studies or a related discipline is required. ABD applicants will be considered as long as all degree requirements are completed by September 1, 2027. The successful candidate will demonstrate evidence of teaching effectiveness, a promising research agenda, and the ability to contribute meaningfully to the Interpersonal/Organizational Communication (I/O) pathway of the department\u2019s major in Communication & Media. The I/O pathway is one of three within the Communication & Media major, alongside Media, Culture & Society and Digital Communication & Content Creation. Candidates with expertise in the following specializations of Interpersonal and/or Organizational communication are encouraged to apply: communication in the workplace, relational communication, sports communication, or human-machine/AI-mediated communication. Job Description : The successful candidate will teach a variety of undergraduate courses such as Interpersonal Communication, Organizational Communication, Group Dynamics, Presentational Speaking, and courses in the candidate\u2019s area of expertise, strategically developed in response to student interest and evolving professional needs. Ohio Northern faculty in the College of Arts & Sciences teach 23-25 credit hours per year. Additional responsibilities include advising undergraduate students, scholarship, and service. Please submit the following documents to ensure your application is complete: Cover letter. CV that includes the names and contact information (phone + email) for 3 professional references. Statement of teaching philosophy - please discuss how you would or have supported a classroom of students with a broad cross-section of differing levels of academic preparation. Research agenda involving undergraduates that is suitable for a primarily undergraduate institution. Unofficial transcripts for your undergraduate and graduate degrees. Questions concerning the position should be directed to Dr. Megan Wood at m-wood@onu.edu. The Getty College of Arts & Sciences is proud to focus exclusively on undergraduate education. We place a premium on faculty who provide close mentoring through small classrooms and experiential learning. Our students share a passion for learning that goes beyond the classroom across 35 nationally acclaimed and accredited degree programs. A&S students are fueled by a commitment to make a difference in their local and global communities. The College of Arts & Sciences has an impressive record of professional accomplishments by our alumni. Ohio Northern University ranks in the top 100 private universities in the U.S. ONU is ranked #1 in the state of Ohio for Best Value and #31 in the U.S. for Best Value by U.S. News & World Report . Located in Ada, Ohio, the University\u2019s rural setting provides a rhythm of life that is peaceful and unhurried. The natural beauty of campus and the friendliness of the village and university communities offer an ideal setting for the pursuit of knowledge and genuine relationships. Additional information about Ohio Northern University is available at http://www.onu.edu . Your next professional chapter begins here! ONU is an equal employment opportunity employer. Accordingly, no person shall be discriminated against on the basis of race, color, sex, gender identity, transgender status, religion, national origin, age, disability, sexual orientation, marital status, military or veteran status, genetic information or any other category protected by federal, state, or local law. This policy applies to all areas of employment including recruitment, hiring, training and development, promotion, transfer, compensation, benefits, discipline, separation and other terms, condition and privileges of employment."}, "https://onu.wd501.myworkdayjobs.com/ONU/job/Ohio-Northern-University/Assistant-Professor-of-Chemistry_JR100301": {"title": "Assistant Professor of Chemistry", "description": "Posted: 2026-10-12\nFull time\n\nCareer Opportunities at Ohio Northern University Job Summary: The Department of Chemistry & Biochemistry in the Getty College of Arts & Sciences at Ohio Northern University welcomes applicants for a tenure-track, assistant professor position in Chemistry, specializing in analytical, inorganic, or biochemistry. Applicants with expertise in materials science, toxicology, forensic science, or interdisciplinary fields are encouraged to apply. We seek a talented individual who is (1) passionate about teaching both lower-division and upper-division undergraduate chemistry courses, (2) committed to scholarship that involves undergraduates, and (3) invested in student success. If you desire to make a difference in the lives of undergraduate students, we invite you to apply for a tenure-track faculty position to begin August 17, 2027. Review of applications will begin October 15, 2026 and continue until the position is filled. A Ph.D. in Chemistry or a related discipline is required (ABD will be considered if all degree requirements are completed by September 1, 2027). The successful candidate will demonstrate strong interpersonal skills, as well as the interest and ability to mentor students both inside and outside the classroom. Candidates with experience teaching undergraduate chemistry courses and involvement in undergraduate research are encouraged to apply. Job Description : The successful candidate will teach a variety of undergraduate Chemistry courses. Ohio Northern faculty in the College of Arts & Sciences teach 23-25 credit hours per year. Additional responsibilities include advising undergraduate students, scholarship and mentoring undergraduate research, and service. \u00a0 Please submit the following documents to ensure your application is complete: Cover letter. CV that includes the names and contact information (phone + email) for 3 professional references. Statement of teaching philosophy - please discuss how you would or have supported a classroom of students with a broad cross-section of differing levels of academic preparation. Statement of proposed scholarship that emphasizes suitability of research for undergraduate students and highlights potential funding sources (3-5 pages plus references) Unofficial transcripts for your undergraduate and graduate degrees. Questions concerning the position should be directed to Chair Kelly Hall at k-hall.6 @onu.edu . \u00a0 The Getty College of Arts & Sciences is proud to focus exclusively on undergraduate education. We place a premium on faculty who provide close mentoring through small classrooms and experiential learning. Our students share a passion for learning that goes beyond the classroom across 35 nationally acclaimed and accredited degree programs. A&S students are fueled by a commitment to make a difference in their local and global communities. The College of Arts & Sciences has an impressive record of professional accomplishments by our alumni. Ohio Northern University ranks in the top 100 private universities in the U.S. ONU is ranked #1 in the state of Ohio for Best Value and #31 in the U.S. for Best Value by U.S. News & World Report . Located in Ada, Ohio, the University\u2019s rural setting provides a rhythm of life that is peaceful and unhurried. The natural beauty of campus and the friendliness of the village and university communities offer an ideal setting for the pursuit of knowledge and genuine relationships. Additional information about Ohio Northern University is available at http://www.onu.edu Your next professional chapter begins here! ONU is an equal employment opportunity employer. Accordingly, no person shall be discriminated against on the basis of race, color, sex, gender identity, transgender status, religion, national origin, age, disability, sexual orientation, marital status, military or veteran status, genetic information or any other category protected by federal, state, or local law. This policy applies to all areas of employment including recruitment, hiring, training and development, promotion, transfer, compensation, benefits, discipline, separation and other terms, condition and privileges of employment."}, "https://onu.wd501.myworkdayjobs.com/ONU/job/Ohio-Northern-University/Assistant-Professor-of-Religion_JR100322": {"title": "Assistant Professor of Religion", "description": "Posted: 2026-10-12\nFull time\n\nCareer Opportunities at Ohio Northern University Job Summary: The Department of English, Philosophy & Religion in the Getty College of Arts & Sciences at Ohio Northern University welcomes applicants for a tenure-track, assistant professor position in Religion. We seek a talented individual who is passionate about teaching, invested in student success, and eager to contribute to a dynamic interdisciplinary department. If you desire to make a difference in the lives of undergraduate students, we invite you to apply for a tenure-track faculty position to begin August 17, 2027. Review of applications begin on December 1, 2026 and will continue until the position is filled. The Ph.D. in Religion or a closely related field is required. ABDs will be considered as long as all degree requirements are completed by September 1, 2027. The successful candidate will be a versatile and broadly trained teacher of Christianity, able to offer a wide breadth of courses of interest to a general education audience. The successful candidate will also develop new courses in western religious traditions and religious ethics. The successful candidate will also demonstrate strong interpersonal skills, a collaborative ethos, and an interest in advising undergraduate students and student groups. Job Description : The successful candidate will teach a variety of undergraduate Religion courses that appeal to a university-wide audience and intersect religious study with the professions and experiential learning. Ohio Northern faculty in the College of Arts & Sciences teach 23-25 credit hours per year. Additional responsibilities include advising undergraduate students, scholarship, and service to the department, college, and university. The successful candidate will offer versatility in teaching Religion courses that appeal to a university-wide audience and courses that intersect religious study with the professions and experiential learning. Please submit the following documents to ensure your application is complete: Cover letter that includes a brief proposal for a course that is informed by and extends our current Religion course offerings and offers new horizons for its study. CV that includes the names and contact information (phone + email) for 3 professional references. Statement of teaching philosophy - please discuss how you would or have supported a classroom of students with a broad cross-section of differing levels of academic preparation. Statement of proposed scholarship Unofficial transcripts for your undergraduate and graduate degrees. Questions concerning the position should be directed to Hongyu Wu at h-wu@onu.edu. The Getty College of Arts & Sciences is proud to focus exclusively on undergraduate education. We place a premium on faculty who provide close mentoring through small classrooms and experiential learning. Our students share a passion for learning that goes beyond the classroom across 35 nationally acclaimed and accredited degree programs. A&S students are fueled by a commitment to make a difference in their local and global communities. The College of Arts & Sciences has an impressive record of professional accomplishments by our alumni. Ohio Northern University ranks in the top 100 private universities in the U.S. ONU is ranked #1 in the state of Ohio for Best Value and #31 in the U.S. for Best Value by U.S. News & World Report . Located in Ada, Ohio, the University\u2019s rural setting provides a rhythm of life that is peaceful and unhurried. The natural beauty of campus and the friendliness of the village and university communities offer an ideal setting for the pursuit of knowledge and genuine relationships. Additional information about Ohio Northern University is available at http://www.onu.edu . Your next professional chapter begins here! ONU is an equal employment opportunity employer. Accordingly, no person shall be discriminated against on the basis of race, color, sex, gender identity, transgender status, religion, national origin, age, disability, sexual orientation, marital status, military or veteran status, genetic information or any other category protected by federal, state, or local law. This policy applies to all areas of employment including recruitment, hiring, training and development, promotion, transfer, compensation, benefits, discipline, separation and other terms, condition and privileges of employment."}, "https://onu.wd501.myworkdayjobs.com/ONU/job/Ohio-Northern-University/Assistant-Professor-of-English_JR100321": {"title": "Assistant Professor of English", "description": "Posted: 2026-10-12\nFull time\n\nCareer Opportunities at Ohio Northern University Job Summary: The Department of English, Philosophy & Religion in the Getty College of Arts & Sciences at Ohio Northern University welcomes applicants for a tenure-track, assistant professor position in English. We seek a talented individual who is passionate about teaching, invested in student success, and eager to contribute to a dynamic interdisciplinary department. If you desire to make a difference in the lives of undergraduate students, we invite you to apply for a tenure-track faculty position to begin August 17, 2027. Review of applications begin on December 1, 2026 and will continue until the position is filled. The Ph.D. in English or a closely related discipline is required. ABDs will be considered as long as all degree requirements are completed by September 1, 2027. Field of study is open. Candidates with experience and interest in teaching British literature, Introduction to Film, or teaching undergraduate English courses to a wide range of audiences are encouraged to apply. The successful candidate will be a versatile and broadly trained teacher with experience in teaching and developing courses of relevance for majors in Creative Writing, English, and English Education, as well as courses of interest for students in our general education program. The successful candidate will also demonstrate strong interpersonal skills, a collaborative ethos, and an interest in advising undergraduate students and student groups. Job Description : The successful candidate will teach a variety of undergraduate English courses. Teaching opportunities include literature surveys, film surveys, freshman composition, and other courses based on the candidate\u2019s interest. Ohio Northern faculty in the College of Arts & Sciences teach 23-25 credit hours per year. Additional responsibilities include advising undergraduate students, scholarship, and service to the department, college, and university. Please submit the following documents to ensure your application is complete: Cover letter that includes a brief proposal for a course that is informed by and extends our current English course offerings and offer new horizons for its study CV that includes the names and contact information (phone + email) for 3 professional references. Statement of teaching philosophy - please discuss how you would or have supported a classroom of students with a broad cross-section of differing levels of academic preparation. Statement of proposed scholarship Unofficial transcripts for your undergraduate and graduate degrees. Questions concerning the position should be directed to Bryan Lutz at b-lutz.1@onu.edu. The Getty College of Arts & Sciences is proud to focus exclusively on undergraduate education. We place a premium on faculty who provide close mentoring through small classrooms and experiential learning. Our students share a passion for learning that goes beyond the classroom across 35 nationally acclaimed and accredited degree programs. A&S students are fueled by a commitment to make a difference in their local and global communities. The College of Arts & Sciences has an impressive record of professional accomplishments by our alumni. Ohio Northern University ranks in the top 100 private universities in the U.S. ONU is ranked #1 in the state of Ohio for Best Value and #31 in the U.S. for Best Value by U.S. News & World Report . Located in Ada, Ohio, the University\u2019s rural setting provides a rhythm of life that is peaceful and unhurried. The natural beauty of campus and the friendliness of the village and university communities offer an ideal setting for the pursuit of knowledge and genuine relationships. Additional information about Ohio Northern University is available at http://www.onu.edu . Your next professional chapter begins here! ONU is an equal employment opportunity employer. Accordingly, no person shall be discriminated against on the basis of race, color, sex, gender identity, transgender status, religion, national origin, age, disability, sexual orientation, marital status, military or veteran status, genetic information or any other category protected by federal, state, or local law. This policy applies to all areas of employment including recruitment, hiring, training and development, promotion, transfer, compensation, benefits, discipline, separation and other terms, condition and privileges of employment."}, "https://onu.wd501.myworkdayjobs.com/ONU/job/Ohio-Northern-University/Assistant-or-Associate-Professor-of-Forensic-Biology_JR100320": {"title": "Assistant or Associate Professor of Forensic Biology", "description": "Posted: 2026-10-12\nFull time\n\nCareer Opportunities at Ohio Northern University Job Summary: The Department of Biology in the Getty College of Arts & Sciences at Ohio Northern University welcomes applicants for a renewable (non-tenure track), assistant or associate professor position in Forensic Biology. Rank commensurate with experience. The Forensic Biology program at ONU is ranked #3 by ForensicColleges.Com. Candidates with expertise to teach not only forensic science but also other natural science content areas are encouraged to apply. We seek an individual who is passionate about teaching undergraduate forensic science courses, committed to experiential learning, and invested in student success. If you desire to make a difference in the lives of undergraduate students, we invite you to apply for a renewable (non-tenure track) faculty position to begin August 17, 2027. Review of applications will begin November 15, 2026 and continue until the position is filled. An M.S. plus work experience or a Ph.D. in Forensic Science, Biology, or a related discipline is required. The successful candidate will demonstrate a commitment to inclusive pedagogical strategies that engage today\u2019s students and expose them to emerging AI technologies within forensic science. In addition, the successful candidate will have experience with contemporary and traditional laboratory techniques, strong interpersonal skills, and the interest and ability to mentor students both inside and outside the classroom. Job Description : The successful candidate will be a broadly trained forensic scientist interested in teaching undergraduate courses and providing leadership for internship placement of students. The successful candidate will also offer versatility in teaching or co-teaching other undergraduate natural science courses. Ohio Northern University faculty teach 23-25 credit hours per academic year. Additional responsibilities include advising undergraduate students and service to the department, college, and university. \u00a0 Please submit the following documents to ensure your application is complete: Cover letter CV that includes the names and contact information (phone + email) for 3 professional references. Statement of teaching philosophy - please discuss how you would or have supported a classroom of students with a broad cross-section of differing levels of academic preparation. Unofficial transcripts for your undergraduate and graduate degrees. \u00a0 Questions concerning the position should be directed to Dr. Robert Verb, Chair of the Search Committee, at r-verb@onu.edu . \u00a0 The Getty College of Arts & Sciences is proud to focus exclusively on undergraduate education. We place a premium on faculty who provide close mentoring through small classrooms and experiential learning. Our students share a passion for learning that goes beyond the classroom across 35 nationally acclaimed and accredited degree programs. A&S students are fueled by a commitment to make a difference in their local and global communities. The College of Arts & Sciences has an impressive record of professional accomplishments by our alumni. Ohio Northern University ranks in the top 100 private universities in the U.S. \u00a0ONU is ranked #1 in the state of Ohio for Best Value and #31 in the U.S. for Best Value by U.S. News & World Report . Located in Ada, Ohio, the University\u2019s rural setting provides a rhythm of life that is peaceful and unhurried. The natural beauty of campus and the friendliness of the village and campus communities offer an ideal setting for the pursuit of knowledge and genuine relationships. Additional information about Ohio Northern University is available at http://www.onu.edu . Your next professional chapter begins here! ONU is an equal employment opportunity employer. Accordingly, no person shall be discriminated against on the basis of race, color, sex, gender identity, transgender status, religion, national origin, age, disability, sexual orientation, marital status, military or veteran status, genetic information or any other category protected by federal, state, or local law. This policy applies to all areas of employment including recruitment, hiring, training and development, promotion, transfer, compensation, benefits, discipline, separation and other terms, condition and privileges of employment."}, "https://onu.wd501.myworkdayjobs.com/ONU/job/Ohio-Northern-University/Assistant-Coach-of-Bowling_JR100319": {"title": "Assistant Coach of Bowling", "description": "Posted: 2026-10-07\nPart time\n\nCareer Opportunities at Ohio Northern University Job Summary: The Assistant Bowling Coach works closely with the Head Coach to support the daily operations, development, and overall success of the college bowling program. This position will assist with coaching, player development, recruiting, team activities, and tournament preparation while helping create a positive and competitive team environment. Job Description : Responsibilities Assist with planning and conducting team practices, workouts, and competitions. Provide coaching, instruction, and feedback to student-athletes. Assist with player development, video analysis, lane-play strategy, and game adjustments. Help identify, communicate with, and recruit prospective student-athletes. Travel with the team to tournaments and assist with tournament preparation and coaching. Help manage team bowling equipment, including ball maintenance and preparation. Assist with team communication, team events, fundraising, and other program activities. Promote a positive, competitive, and team-oriented environment. Serve as a positive role model and mentor for student-athletes. Support the academic, athletic, and personal development of team members. Work closely with the Head Coach to help achieve the goals and vision of the bowling program. Perform other duties as assigned by the Head Coach. Qualifications Collegiate coaching experience preferred. USBC Silver certification/training preferred. Strong knowledge of bowling fundamentals, equipment, and competitive strategy. Strong communication and organizational skills. Your next professional chapter begins here! ONU is an equal employment opportunity employer. Accordingly, no person shall be discriminated against on the basis of race, color, sex, gender identity, transgender status, religion, national origin, age, disability, sexual orientation, marital status, military or veteran status, genetic information or any other category protected by federal, state, or local law. This policy applies to all areas of employment including recruitment, hiring, training and development, promotion, transfer, compensation, benefits, discipline, separation and other terms, condition and privileges of employment."}, "https://onu.wd501.myworkdayjobs.com/ONU/job/Ohio-Northern-University/Assistant-Professor-of-Sport-Management_JR100312": {"title": "Assistant Professor of Sport Management", "description": "Posted: 2026-10-01\nFull time\n\nCareer Opportunities at Ohio Northern University Job Summary: The Dicke College of Business Administration at Ohio Northern University welcomes applicants for a non-tenure, renewable-track, assistant professor position in Sport Management. We seek a talented individual who is (1) passionate about teaching both lower-division and upper-division undergraduate Sport Management courses, (2) committed to scholarship that involves undergraduates, and (3) invested in student success. If you desire to make a difference in the lives of undergraduate students, we invite you to apply for a renewable-track faculty position to begin August 17, 2027. Review of applications will begin October 5, 2026 and continue until the position is filled. A Ph.D.or ABD in Sport Management or a related discipline is required. The successful candidate will demonstrate a commitment to excellence in undergraduate teaching and academic advising, possessing excellent teaching and mentoring skills as well as evidence of research and or publications in peer reviewed journals that would qualify the applicant for rank of Assistant Professor. Job Description : The successful candidate will teach a variety of undergraduate Sport Management courses, including principles of sport management and upper-level sport management topics, as well as other areas consistent with the candidate\u2019s professional background. Scholarly research and publication are expected. Additional responsibilities include advising undergraduate students, scholarship and mentoring undergraduate research, and service. In your statement of teaching philosophy, please discuss how you would or have supported a classroom of students with a broad cross-section of differing levels of academic preparation. Please ensure your CV includes the names and contact information (phone + email) for 3 professional references. Questions concerning the position should be directed to Dean John Navin at j-navin@onu.edu The Dicke College of Business Administration is proud to focus exclusively on undergraduate education. We place a premium on faculty who provide close mentoring through small classrooms and experiential learning. Our students share a passion for learning that goes beyond the classroom across 7 accredited degree programs by the Association to Advance Collegiate Schools of Business. Our students are fueled by a commitment to make a difference in their local and global communities. The Dicke College of Business Administration has an impressive record of professional accomplishments by our alumni. U.S. News & World Report has named Ohio Northern University one of the nation\u2019s top 100 private universities and awarded it the #31 spot nationally and #1 in the state of Ohio for Best Value Schools. Located in Ada, Ohio, the University\u2019s rural setting provides a rhythm of life that is peaceful and unhurried. The natural beauty of campus and the friendliness of the village and university communities offer an ideal setting for the pursuit of knowledge and genuine relationships. Additional information about Ohio Northern University is available at http://www.onu.edu . Your next professional chapter begins here! ONU is an equal employment opportunity employer. Accordingly, no person shall be discriminated against on the basis of race, color, sex, gender identity, transgender status, religion, national origin, age, disability, sexual orientation, marital status, military or veteran status, genetic information or any other category protected by federal, state, or local law. This policy applies to all areas of employment including recruitment, hiring, training and development, promotion, transfer, compensation, benefits, discipline, separation and other terms, condition and privileges of employment."}, "https://onu.wd501.myworkdayjobs.com/ONU/job/Ohio-Northern-University/Assistant-Coach-of-Men-s-Lacrosse_JR100311": {"title": "Assistant Coach of Men's Lacrosse", "description": "Posted: 2026-10-01\nFull time\n\nCareer Opportunities at Ohio Northern University Job Summary: Support the Athletic Department through serving as an Assistant Lacrosse Coach. Job Description : Assistant Lacrosse coaching duties will be as assigned by head coach and will include administration, coaching, and recruiting for the ONU Lacrosse program and other duties as assigned. Required Skills: Advanced knowledge of professional theories and practices within the given field and a working knowledge of related fields. Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor\u2019s Degree.\u00a0 Coaching experience in Lacrosse. Your next professional chapter begins here! ONU is an equal employment opportunity employer. Accordingly, no person shall be discriminated against on the basis of race, color, sex, gender identity, transgender status, religion, national origin, age, disability, sexual orientation, marital status, military or veteran status, genetic information or any other category protected by federal, state, or local law. This policy applies to all areas of employment including recruitment, hiring, training and development, promotion, transfer, compensation, benefits, discipline, separation and other terms, condition and privileges of employment."}, "https://onu.wd501.myworkdayjobs.com/ONU/job/Ohio-Northern-University/Senior-Administrative-Assistant_JR100279": {"title": "Senior Administrative Assistant", "description": "Posted: 2026-09-25\nFull time\n\nCareer Opportunities at Ohio Northern University Job Summary: This position provides comprehensive administrative support to the Director of Student Services and the Associate Dean of Academic Affairs and serves as the primary administrative liaison for the College of Law\u2019s in-person faculty. The role supports the day-to-day operations of Student Services and Academic Affairs, including academic processes, faculty support, student programming and services, scheduling, records and documentation, event coordination, and general administrative operations. This position requires strong organizational skills, attention to detail, the ability to manage multiple priorities, and independent judgment in coordinating the needs of students, faculty, and law school administration. Job Description : Position Summary The Administrative Assistant provides comprehensive administrative and operational support to the Director of Student Services and the Associate Dean of Academic Affairs and serves as a primary administrative resource for the College of Law\u2019s in-person faculty. The position plays an important role in the day-to-day operations of the College of Law, supporting academic administration, faculty needs, student services, programs and events, and other Dean\u2019s Office functions. This position requires a high level of organization, attention to detail, discretion, independent judgment, and the ability to manage multiple priorities and deadlines throughout the academic year. The Administrative Assistant regularly works with confidential student, faculty, and academic information and coordinates with departments throughout the University as well as outside vendors, speakers, guests, and organizations. Essential Duties and Responsibilities Academic Affairs and Student Records Provide administrative support for the College of Law\u2019s academic operations, including course scheduling, registration, advising, grades, academic standing, rankings, graduation, and related academic processes. Prepare and maintain course schedules, conflict charts, registration and advising materials, faculty advisor assignments, registration information, exam numbers, and other academic records and materials as assigned. Assist with grade processing and related academic records, including grade entry, GPA and class rankings, Dean\u2019s List, academic standing information, and student records maintained by the College of Law. Assist the Associate Dean of Academic Affairs with identifying and tracking students subject to academic policies, including scheduling meetings and preparing correspondence related to academic standing, dismissal, readmission, and other academic matters. Prepare and process graduation-related academic documentation, including law school certificates, final academic certifications, and documentation required by bar examining authorities. Process letters of good standing and other academic documentation requested by students or graduates. Maintain accurate and confidential academic records and coordinate with the University Registrar and other University offices as necessary. Academic Scheduling and Registration Provide administrative support to the Associate Dean of Academic Affairs in the development and administration of the academic schedule for Fall, Spring, Summer, and J-Term. Prepare and maintain course conflict charts, registration materials, advising packets, course offerings, schedules, and related academic information. Assist with registration processes, including coordination with students, faculty advisors, the Registrar\u2019s Office, and other University departments. Assist with preparation and submission of course and scheduling information required by the University. Coordinate recurring administrative components of registration and advising to ensure materials are prepared and deadlines are met. Faculty and Academic Administration Serve as a primary administrative resource for the College of Law\u2019s in-person faculty and provide day-to-day administrative support related to teaching, academic responsibilities, and general faculty needs. Provide administrative support to the Dean\u2019s Coordinator in coordinating faculty meetings, including scheduling, preparation and distribution of agendas and materials, and other meeting-related needs. Provide administrative support to the Dean and Associate Dean of Academic Affairs with faculty and adjunct processes, including adjunct requests, faculty evaluations, course evaluation records, overload and extra-earnings documentation, and other faculty-related materials. Assist with faculty teaching assignments, administrative assignments, faculty advisor assignments, semester preparation, and academic calendars. Provide administrative assistance with faculty committees and academic governance processes, including committee materials, promotion and tenure documentation, and other responsibilities as assigned by the Dean or Associate Dean of Academic Affairs. Coordinate recurring faculty administrative needs such as book orders, mailboxes, communications, records, and instructional materials. Assist with onboarding new faculty and provide administrative support related to faculty transitions. Student Services, Programs and Events Provide administrative and logistical support to the Director of Student Services in the planning and execution of College of Law programs, student activities, lectures, competitions, ceremonies, and special events. Assist with event logistics, including room reservations, catering and food orders, setup and breakdown, supplies, signage, guest arrangements, schedules, communications, registration materials, and coordination with University departments and outside vendors. Assist with major College of Law events and programs, which may include Orientation, Homecoming, Honors Day, Commencement, the 3L BBQ, Willis Society events, lectures and speaker programs, student competitions, student organization programming, and other events throughout the academic year. Provide administrative and logistical support for moot court, mock trial, and other student competitions as assigned, including registrations, scheduling, travel documentation, lodging, and related arrangements. Assist with student communications, preparation of program and event materials, maintenance of calendars, room scheduling, and other Student Services administrative needs. Provide on-site support before and during programs and events as needed and assist with resolving logistical issues that arise. Bar, Graduation and Academic Certification Maintain information related to graduates and bar examination participation and assist with preparation of bar passage information and reports. Prepare and process certificates, letters of good standing, final law school certifications, and other documentation requested by students, graduates, bar examining authorities, and other appropriate entities. Assist the Dean and Associate Dean of Academic Affairs with tracking and reporting bar examination results and related information. Maintain graduation and bar-related records and coordinate the submission of required documentation following the posting of final grades. Dean\u2019s Office and College Operations Provide administrative support to the Director of Student Services and Associate Dean of Academic Affairs and assist with the overall daily operations of the Dean\u2019s Office. Work collaboratively with the Dean\u2019s Coordinator and other Dean\u2019s Office staff to provide administrative coverage and support for faculty, students, and law school administration. Serve as a point of contact for students, faculty, staff, University departments, vendors, guests, and other individuals working with the College of Law and direct questions or requests to the appropriate individual when necessary. Maintain files, records, directories, calendars, mailboxes, shared documents, and other administrative systems. Prepare correspondence, memoranda, reports, spreadsheets, forms, and other materials in support of law school administration. Provide administrative support for annual reports, accreditation and ABA reporting, University reporting requirements, and the collection and organization of supporting information. Assist with purchasing, payment documentation, travel documentation, supplies, and other administrative transactions as assigned. General Responsibilities Maintain confidentiality of student educational records, personnel information, academic records, grades, faculty information, and other sensitive or confidential information. Communicate professionally and effectively with students, faculty, staff, alumni, University offices, courts, bar authorities, vendors, and outside organizations. Develop and maintain organized systems for recurring academic, student services, faculty, and administrative processes and ensure established deadlines are met. Exercise independent judgment in prioritizing work, resolving routine administrative issues, identifying information needed to complete assigned processes, and determining when matters should be elevated to the appropriate administrator. Work collaboratively with the Director of Student Services, Associate Dean of Academic Affairs, Dean\u2019s Coordinator, Dean, and other College of Law staff to anticipate upcoming deadlines, events, academic processes, and operational needs. Provide cross-functional administrative support within the Dean\u2019s Office and assist with additional projects and responsibilities as needed. Perform other duties as assigned. Knowledge, Skills and Abilities Strong organizational and time-management skills with the ability to manage multiple projects, recurring processes, events, and competing deadlines. Exceptional attention to detail and accuracy, particularly when working with academic records, grades, rankings, schedules, financial documentation, and student information. Ability to exercise discretion and maintain confidentiality when handling sensitive student, faculty, personnel, and institutional information. Strong written and verbal communication skills and the ability to interact professionally with students, faculty, administrators, University offices, vendors, guests, and outside organizations. Ability to work independently, anticipate administrative and logistical needs, solve routine problems, and exercise sound judgment. Ability to understand, follow, and administer established academic and University procedures and recognize when a matter requires review or decision by the appropriate administrator. Strong computer skills and the ability to learn and utilize University systems, databases, scheduling platforms, spreadsheets, document-management systems, and other technology used by the College of Law. Ability to coordinate multiple individuals, departments, vendors, deadlines, and logistical details. Ability to work effectively in a fast-paced academic environment with periods of significant deadline-driven activity throughout the academic year. Your next professional chapter begins here! ONU is an equal employment opportunity employer. Accordingly, no person shall be discriminated against on the basis of race, color, sex, gender identity, transgender status, religion, national origin, age, disability, sexual orientation, marital status, military or veteran status, genetic information or any other category protected by federal, state, or local law. This policy applies to all areas of employment including recruitment, hiring, training and development, promotion, transfer, compensation, benefits, discipline, separation and other terms, condition and privileges of employment."}, "https://onu.wd501.myworkdayjobs.com/ONU/job/Ohio-Northern-University/Director-of-Education-Licensure---Accreditation_JR100307": {"title": "Director of Education Licensure & Accreditation", "description": "Posted: 2026-09-25\nFull time\n\nCareer Opportunities at Ohio Northern University Job Summary: The Department of Psychology & Education in the Getty College of Arts & Sciences at Ohio Northern University welcomes applicants to serve as the Director of Education Licensure & Accreditation. We seek a talented individual who is passionate about the preparation of undergraduate pre-service teachers and invested in student success. If you desire to make a difference in the lives of undergraduate students, we invite you to apply for a 12-month position to begin no later than August 17, 2027. Review of applications will begin on October 15, 2026 and continue until the position is filled. A master\u2019s degree in Education, Data Analytics, Social Sciences, or a related field requiring statistical or curricular evaluation is required. A minimum of 3 years\u2019 experience managing institutional data collection, quantitative or qualitative data analysis, or coordinating professional accreditation cycles is required. Candidates with an earned doctorate (Ph.D. or Ed.D.) in an education-related field, experience directly interfacing with the Council for the Accreditation of Educator Preparation (CAEP) and the Ohio Department of Higher Education (ODHE), or a minimum of 3 years\u2019 teaching in a K-12 classroom are encouraged to apply. Job Description : The successful candidate will demonstrate strong organizational, technology, interpersonal, and communication skills to manage complex feedback loops and articulate assessment results to diverse academic groups. \u00a0 The successful candidate will teach one course per semester, manage assessment systems, coordinate data collection for continuous program improvement, and lead professional, state, and regional accreditation processes for educator preparation programs.\u00a0 Licensure & Accreditation: Lead the planning, preparation, and submission of self-study reports and degree verification, including comprehensive evidence files and standards alignment, for the State of Ohio (ODHE) and the Council for the Accreditation of Educator Preparation (CAEP). Assessment Management: Map curriculum components to ODHE regulations and CAEP standards. Collaborate with program faculty and staff to design, monitor, and refine systematic assessment plans for evaluating student learning outcomes. Construct assessment timelines and deploy evaluation rubrics. Collaborate with the Director of Academic Assessment in the Office of Academic Affairs. Data Systems, Analysis & Reporting: Collect, manage, and interpret student learning outcome data. Build and manage systematic feedback loops. Analyze enrollment, retention, and performance metrics to generate actionable assessment briefs for the school director, dean, and provost. Stakeholder Communication & Collaboration: Communicate assessment outcomes clearly and work closely with faculty, staff, university committees, institutional research, and external stakeholders to integrate and streamline assessment and evaluation practices. \u00a0 Application Instructions: 1. Cover Letter: Detailed letter describing direct experience with structural program assessment, state frameworks, and multi-layered accreditation cycles. 2.\u00a0\u00a0 Resume / CV: Full professional history reflecting administrative metrics and systems leadership. Names and contact information (email and phone) for 3 professional references. 3.\u00a0\u00a0 Data Writing Sample: A short sample showing the ability to translate technical statistical data or evaluation rubrics into accessible summaries for internal faculty or external review boards. Questions concerning the position should be directed to the Search Committee Chair, Dr. Kyle Harris at k-harris.4@onu.edu. The Getty College of Arts & Sciences is proud to focus exclusively on undergraduate education. We place a premium on faculty who provide close mentoring in small classroom settings and through experiential learning. Our students share a passion for learning that goes beyond the classroom across 35 nationally acclaimed and accredited degree programs. A&S students are fueled by a commitment to make a difference in their local and global communities. The College of Arts & Sciences has an impressive record of professional accomplishments by our alumni. Ohio Northern University is ranked #1 in the state of Ohio for Best Value by both the Wall Street Journal and U.S. News & World Report . Located in Ada, Ohio, the University\u2019s rural setting provides a rhythm of life that is peaceful and unhurried. The natural beauty of campus and the friendliness of the village and university communities offer an ideal setting for the pursuit of knowledge and genuine relationships. Additional information about Ohio Northern University is available at http://www.onu.edu . Your next professional chapter begins here! ONU is an equal employment opportunity employer. Accordingly, no person shall be discriminated against on the basis of race, color, sex, gender identity, transgender status, religion, national origin, age, disability, sexual orientation, marital status, military or veteran status, genetic information or any other category protected by federal, state, or local law. This policy applies to all areas of employment including recruitment, hiring, training and development, promotion, transfer, compensation, benefits, discipline, separation and other terms, condition and privileges of employment."}, "https://onu.wd501.myworkdayjobs.com/ONU/job/Ohio-Northern-University/Vice-President-for-Enrollment-Management_JR100252": {"title": "Vice President for Enrollment Management", "description": "Posted: 2026-09-14\nFull time\n\nCareer Opportunities at Ohio Northern University Job Summary: Ohio Northern University, an independent, selective, comprehensive university located in Northwest, Ohio, announces the search for a strategic Vice President for Enrollment Management (VPEM). The Vice President for Enrollment Management serves as a key member of the President\u2019s Cabinet, reporting directly to the President. This senior leadership role provides strategic oversight and direction for all enrollment management operations, ensuring alignment with the University\u2019s mission, financial objectives, and commitment to building an academically strong and multi-talented student body. Job Description : THE POSITION The VPEM is responsible for leading the University\u2019s enrollment strategy, encompassing student recruitment, admissions, financial aid, and enrollment planning. Working collaboratively, the Vice President drives initiatives to meet or exceed enrollment targets, achieve net tuition revenue goals, and enhance the quality and breadth of applicant pools. Through collaborative partnerships across the University, especially with the Vice President for Financial Affairs (VPFA), the Provost, Deans, and the Athletic Director, the VPEM ensures a coordinated, data-driven approach to recruiting, retaining, and graduating students from varied backgrounds. Full Position Announcement: https://nessearches.com/onu-vpem/ COMPENSATION Compensation for the position will be competitive and based on the skills and experience of the selected candidate and the agreed upon portfolio of responsibilities; consult with the NES search team for insights. Additionally, Ohio Northern University offers a comprehensive package of benefits. Given the nature of this visible campus and community-based leadership position, the selected candidate will be expected to reside in or near Ada, Ohio. To Apply NES , a higher education search firm specializing in enrollment management searches, is assisting Ohio Northern in identifying the University's next Vice President for Enrollment Management. For more information, or to nominate someone for this position, contact Laura Robinson ( laura.robinson@nessearches.com ) or Catherine Capolupo ( catherine.capolupo@nessearches.com ). All conversations will remain confidential unless otherwise stated and agreed. Interested candidates should submit a r\u00e9sum\u00e9 and a letter of interest describing their unique qualifications for the Vice President for Enrollment Management position at Ohio Northern University. Candidates should also provide the names and contact information of at least five professional references. For confidentiality, references will not be contacted without permission. All application materials should be submitted electronically to ONU@nessearches.com ; applications will be reviewed on an ongoing basis. The position is campus-based and the preferred start date is January of 2027. Your next professional chapter begins here! ONU is an equal employment opportunity employer. Accordingly, no person shall be discriminated against on the basis of race, color, sex, gender identity, transgender status, religion, national origin, age, disability, sexual orientation, marital status, military or veteran status, genetic information or any other category protected by federal, state, or local law. This policy applies to all areas of employment including recruitment, hiring, training and development, promotion, transfer, compensation, benefits, discipline, separation and other terms, condition and privileges of employment."}, "https://onu.wd501.myworkdayjobs.com/ONU/job/Ohio-Northern-University/Human-Resources-Generalist_JR100238": {"title": "Human Resources Generalist", "description": "Posted: 2026-08-27\nFull time\n\nCareer Opportunities at Ohio Northern University Job Summary: This position is a key member of the Ohio Northern University (ONU) Human Resources (HR) team and provides broad HR support, with a primary focus on employee benefits and payroll administration. Job Description : The position provides comprehensive human resources support with primary responsibility for the administration and oversight of University payroll and employee benefit programs. This role ensures payroll and benefits processes are accurate, timely, compliant, and effectively administered, including enrollment, reconciliation, audits, vendor coordination, claims, and annual open enrollment. The position leads and supports HR projects aligned with departmental and University priorities, including the implementation and enhancement of programs, processes, technologies, policies, and compliance requirements. Additionally, the role serves as a trusted HR resource to employees, supervisors, and the HR team by providing guidance, reporting, process improvement, system administration, and maintaining accurate, confidential, and compliant HR records and documentation.\u00a0 Primary Responsibilities: Oversee payroll and benefits administration to ensure accurate, timely, and compliant processing in accordance with University policies and applicable laws and regulations. Administer employee benefit programs, including assistance with program design, enrollment, payroll reconciliation, claims, audits, vendor coordination, compliance, and annual open enrollment. Serve as a resource to employees and supervisors regarding payroll, benefits, timekeeping, policies, procedures, and related matters while maintaining accurate and confidential records. Lead and support HR projects aligned with departmental and University priorities, including implementation of new programs, processes, technologies, and compliance requirements. Research, develop, and maintain HR policies, procedures, forms, communications, reports, and process documentation, with a focus on benefits, payroll, HR systems, and data integrity. Serve as a general HR resource and provide cross-functional support to employees, supervisors, and the HR team, including reporting, compliance activities, process improvement, system administration, and additional responsibilities as needed. Will have direct supervisory responsibilities within the HR department. Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor\u2019s degree in Human Resources, Business Administration, Accounting, Finance, or related field; equivalent education and relevant experience may be considered. Two to four years of progressive experience in HR, payroll, benefits administration, or a related field, with knowledge of payroll practices, benefits programs, and applicable employment requirements. Strong attention to detail, discretion, and ability to manage confidential information while effectively communicating complex HR, payroll, and benefits matters to employees and managers. Preferred Qualifications: Experience with Workday, particularly Payroll, Benefits, Time Tracking, or related HR functionality. Experience working in higher education Professional HR certification such as SHRM-CP, SHRM-SCP, PHR, or SPHR. Payroll certification or specialized benefits training. Your next professional chapter begins here! ONU is an equal employment opportunity employer. Accordingly, no person shall be discriminated against on the basis of race, color, sex, gender identity, transgender status, religion, national origin, age, disability, sexual orientation, marital status, military or veteran status, genetic information or any other category protected by federal, state, or local law. This policy applies to all areas of employment including recruitment, hiring, training and development, promotion, transfer, compensation, benefits, discipline, separation and other terms, condition and privileges of employment."}, "https://onu.wd501.myworkdayjobs.com/ONU/job/Ohio-Northern-University/Adjunct-Instructor-of-Law_JR100232": {"title": "Adjunct Instructor of Law", "description": "Posted: 2026-08-27\nPart time\n\nCareer Opportunities at Ohio Northern University Job Summary: Ohio Northern University welcomes applicants for a part-time, adjunct faculty position. Job Description : We seek an individual passionate about teaching and invested in student success. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue in order to fill positions as needed each semester. Your next professional chapter begins here! ONU is an equal employment opportunity employer. Accordingly, no person shall be discriminated against on the basis of race, color, sex, gender identity, transgender status, religion, national origin, age, disability, sexual orientation, marital status, military or veteran status, genetic information or any other category protected by federal, state, or local law. This policy applies to all areas of employment including recruitment, hiring, training and development, promotion, transfer, compensation, benefits, discipline, separation and other terms, condition and privileges of employment."}, "https://onu.wd501.myworkdayjobs.com/ONU/job/Ohio-Northern-University/Public-Safety-Officer_JR100183": {"title": "Public Safety Officer", "description": "Posted: 2026-08-20\nFull time\n\nCareer Opportunities at Ohio Northern University Job Summary: This position is responsible for protecting members of the University Community, maintaining order, enforcing policies and procedures, rules and regulations of the Ohio Northern University. Public Safety officers may be assigned to uniform or plainclothes details. Shift scheduling changes periodically, sometimes with little advanced notice in emergency situations. Duties require initiative, resourcefulness and the ability to analyze situations and in emergencies to adopt a quick, effective and responsible course of action. The work involves frequent contact with the public and requires the ability to deal with persons in tense situations where attitudes and relations are strained. Job Description : - Patrols designated areas via motor vehicle, bicycle or on foot to detect criminal activity; inspects doors, windows and premises of University buildings and properties; to detect suspicious vehicles, persons or situations ; maintains high visibility. - Responds to calls for service including domestic situations, assaults, burglaries, thefts, property damage, alarms, bomb threats, natural disasters that affect campus, public service duties such as escorts, vehicle lockouts and door unlocks. - Conducts preliminary/ follow up investigations of complaints or incidents on University property, involving University students, faculty, staff or visitors to campus. - Take fingerprints for background checks. - May be asked to testify in court when subpoenaed; escort law enforcement officers or investigators on campus for various situations; provides assistance or backup to public service agencies including fire and EMS on campus and provide twenty-four hour service to Ohio Northern University. - Operates a variety of standard and specialized equipment and tools associated with public safety including vehicles, OC spray, handcuffs, asp baton, flashlights, fire extinguishers, photographic equipment, telephones, radios, desktop computers, tablets and general office equipment. - Inspects and maintains assigned vehicles and related equipment assigned to public safety vehicles. - Follows safety procedures, utilizes equipment, monitors work environment to ensure the safety of University faculty, staff,students and visitors; Performs driving functions in a safe and efficient manner under various conditions and in adverse weather conditions. - Prepares and completes required forms, reports, correspondence, logs, event reports, damage reports, narratives, missing persons reports, parking registrations and enforces parking regulations on all University lots. - Enters reports directly into ReportExec RMS, using a computer and its accompanying equipment such as a computer and mouse. - Communicates in person, via telephone and/or radio, provides assistance and information to those needing help. - Creates/ maintains positive public relations with the University community and visitors to our campus; Maintains and promotes peace and order; Provides education and information regarding University policies and procedures, personal safety, drug abuse and the law, alcohol laws, crime prevention and other public safety issues. - Attends shift meetings, training sessions both on and off campus, seminars as required to remain knowledgeable of departmental/ University operations and activities, to promote improved job performance and to stay current with trends in the field of public safety. - Other duties as assigned. Qualifications: - High school diploma or GED equivalent - Possess a valid Ohio driver's license - Must be at least 21 years of age - Must be able to successfully complete an approved Ohio Peace Officer Training Private Security Firearms Course within 90 days of employment or a time approved by the Chief of Public Safety if the time exceeds the 90 days based on class availability. Preferred Qualifications: - Ohio Peace Officer training or military equivalent experience - Fire service or EMS background - Professional Security Officer certifications Your next professional chapter begins here! ONU is an equal employment opportunity employer. Accordingly, no person shall be discriminated against on the basis of race, color, sex, gender identity, transgender status, religion, national origin, age, disability, sexual orientation, marital status, military or veteran status, genetic information or any other category protected by federal, state, or local law. This policy applies to all areas of employment including recruitment, hiring, training and development, promotion, transfer, compensation, benefits, discipline, separation and other terms, condition and privileges of employment."}, "https://onu.wd501.myworkdayjobs.com/ONU/job/Ohio-Northern-University/Assistant-Director-of-Residence-Life_JR100170": {"title": "Assistant Director of Residence Life", "description": "Posted: 2026-08-18\nFull time\n\nCareer Opportunities at Ohio Northern University Job Summary: The Assistant Director provides on-campus support to a 2200 bed community. The Assistant Director serves as the primary coordinator of residential programming, departmental assessment, training initiatives and electronic/web communication. This position is live-on. A fully furnished university apartment that includes utilities is provided. Residence Life experience required. Job Description : - Serve as an ambassador/liaison for the Office of Residence Life and Division of Student Affairs. - Assist Director with development/implementation of annual goals, training initiatives, calendar development, assessment strategies and fulfilling department/division objectives. - Oversee the recruitment, selection, training and supervision of all para-professional staff (Resident Directors, Senior Resident Assistants, & Resident Assistants) & summer staff (ex. Clery Act compliance, systems operation, check-in & check-outs, etc.). - Implement campus wide programming initiatives for traditional and non-traditional populations. - Develop marketing initiatives for the office via social media and advertisements. - Assist with Homecoming planning. -Assist in the development and administration of assessment initiatives for the Office of Residence Life in connection with department/division/campus wide Student Learning Outcomes. - Coordinate and implement paraprofessional staff training initiatives for Division of Student Affairs. - Serve on designated committees and initiatives for the division of Student Affairs. - Work directly with web-based housing software (e.g. room selection, reports, etc.). - Manage and update the Office of Residence Life webpage and other social media outlets. - Attend weekly residence life staff meeting with 12 paraprofessional Resident Directors. - Co-facilitate opening and closing of residential areas and other administrative functions. - Fulfill responsibilities of the Director and Housing Coordinator in his/her absence. - Develop and coordinate desk operations where applicable. - Provide on-call coverage as the Professional Staff On-Call on a rotating basis with Director. - Serve as a core member of the Care Team, reaching out to students and completing wellness checks, and attending weekly Care Team meetings - Availability to work evenings and weekends as needed. -Interpersonal Communication & Public Speaking ability. - Other duties and responsibilities as assigned. Your next professional chapter begins here! ONU is an equal employment opportunity employer. Accordingly, no person shall be discriminated against on the basis of race, color, sex, gender identity, transgender status, religion, national origin, age, disability, sexual orientation, marital status, military or veteran status, genetic information or any other category protected by federal, state, or local law. This policy applies to all areas of employment including recruitment, hiring, training and development, promotion, transfer, compensation, benefits, discipline, separation and other terms, condition and privileges of employment."}, "https://onu.wd501.myworkdayjobs.com/ONU/job/Ohio-Northern-University/Assistant-Director-of-Academic-Success--Rank-of-Instructor_JR100141": {"title": "Assistant Director of Academic Success; Rank of Instructor", "description": "Posted: 2026-08-04\nFull time\n\nCareer Opportunities at Ohio Northern University Job Summary: Assistant Director of Academic Success. Non-tenure Track Faculty. 12-month appointment with eligibility for continuing appointment. Instructor Status. The Ohio Northern University Pettit College of Law is seeking to appoint an Assistant Director of Academic Success. Job Description : The Assistant Director will lead the academic support program at ONU and coordinate with and report to the Associate Dean for Academic Affairs to provide an integrated program of academic support and bar support services. The Assistant Director will be an integral part of the Academic Success Program (ASP) at Ohio Northern University College of Law, working with the Associate Dean for Academic Affairs and the Assistant Director for Bar Passage by: Designing and implementing strategies to successfully assist all students' learning, particularly in areas of essay writing, reading comprehension, issue spotting, and legal analysis; Designing and implementing strategies to successfully assist at-risk and high-risk students through individual instruction and by teaching academic support-related courses, including hosting weekly ASP sessions in the Summer Starter Program; Assisting in designing and implementing the academic support component of orientation programs and coordinating and teaching in the January term to first-year students; Hiring, training, and supervising the teaching assistants in the ASP; Evaluating and creating, along with other members of the administration, reports on statistical data regarding students' academic performance and providing input regarding the effectiveness of ASP programs and initiatives. Required Skills: Strong writing, analytical, and organizational skills Strong interpersonal skills including the ability to communicate with groups of students Minimum Qualifications: Candidates must hold at least a J.D. from an ABA accredited law school with a minimum of more than one year\u2019s prior experience in academic support. Your next professional chapter begins here! ONU is an equal employment opportunity employer. Accordingly, no person shall be discriminated against on the basis of race, color, sex, gender identity, transgender status, religion, national origin, age, disability, sexual orientation, marital status, military or veteran status, genetic information or any other category protected by federal, state, or local law. This policy applies to all areas of employment including recruitment, hiring, training and development, promotion, transfer, compensation, benefits, discipline, separation and other terms, condition and privileges of employment."}, "https://onu.wd501.myworkdayjobs.com/ONU/job/Ohio-Northern-University/Adjunct-Instructor-of-Biology_JR100101": {"title": "Adjunct Instructor of Biology", "description": "Posted: 2026-07-29\nPart time\n\nCareer Opportunities at Ohio Northern University Job Summary: The Department of Biology in the Getty College of Arts & Sciences at Ohio Northern University welcomes applicants for a part-time, adjunct faculty position in Biology. Candidates with backgrounds in all areas of Biology will be considered. We seek individuals who are passionate about teaching and invested in student success. If you desire to make a difference in the lives of undergraduate students, we invite you to apply for an adjunct faculty position in Biology. If you desire to make a difference in the lives of undergraduate students, we invite you to apply. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue in order to fill positions as needed each fall and each spring semester. A master\u2019s degree in Biology or 18 hours graduate coursework in Biology is required. Candidates with doctoral degrees in Biology and experience teaching Biology at the university level are encouraged to apply. The successful candidate will demonstrate good interpersonal skills, as well as the interest and ability to mentor students. Please ensure that your CV includes the names and contact information (phone + email) for 3 professional references. Job Description : Successful candidates will serve as instructors of record for introductory lecture courses, laboratories, or other courses as assigned. Typical assignments include one or two courses each semester, depending on student demand. Questions concerning the position should be directed to the Department Chair, Dr. Leslie Riley at l-riley.1@onu.edu. The Getty College of Arts & Sciences is proud to focus exclusively on undergraduate education. We place a premium on faculty providing close mentoring through small classrooms and experiential learning. Our students share a passion for learning that goes beyond the classroom across 35 nationally acclaimed and accredited degree programs. A&S students are fueled by a commitment to making a difference in their local and global communities. The College of Arts & Sciences has an impressive record of professional accomplishments by our alumni. Ohio Northern University is ranked #1 in the state of Ohio for Best Value by both the Wall Street Journal and U.S. News & World Report . Located in Ada, Ohio, the University\u2019s rural setting provides a rhythm of life that is peaceful and unhurried. The natural beauty of campus and friendliness of the village and campus communities offer an ideal setting for the pursuit of knowledge and genuine relationships. Additional information about Ohio Northern University is available at http://www.onu.edu . Your next professional chapter begins here! ONU is an equal employment opportunity employer. Accordingly, no person shall be discriminated against on the basis of race, color, sex, gender identity, transgender status, religion, national origin, age, disability, sexual orientation, marital status, military or veteran status, genetic information or any other category protected by federal, state, or local law. This policy applies to all areas of employment including recruitment, hiring, training and development, promotion, transfer, compensation, benefits, discipline, separation and other terms, condition and privileges of employment."}, "https://onu.wd501.myworkdayjobs.com/ONU/job/Ohio-Northern-University/Adjunct-Instructor-of-Statistics_JR100132": {"title": "Adjunct Instructor of Statistics", "description": "Posted: 2026-07-29\nPart time\n\nCareer Opportunities at Ohio Northern University Job Summary: The Department of Statistics & Applied Technology in the Getty College of Arts & Sciences at Ohio Northern University welcomes applicants for a part-time, adjunct faculty position in Statistics. Candidates with backgrounds in all areas of Statistics will be considered. We seek a talented individual who is passionate about teaching introductory undergraduate statistics courses and invested in student success. If you desire to make a difference in the lives of undergraduate students, we invite you to apply. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue in order to fill positions as needed each fall and each spring semester. A master\u2019s degree in Statistics or 18 hours graduate coursework in Statistics is required. Candidates with doctoral degrees in Statistics and experience teaching Statistics at the university level are encouraged to apply. The successful candidate will demonstrate good interpersonal skills, as well as the interest and ability to mentor students. Please ensure that your CV includes the names and contact information (phone + email) for 3 professional references. Job Description : Successful candidates will serve as instructors of record for introductory statistics courses or other courses as assigned. Assignments typically consist of one, two, or three courses per semester. Questions concerning the position should be directed to the Director of the School for Mathematical & Physical Sciences, Dr. Tevye Celius at t-celius@onu.edu. The Getty College of Arts & Sciences is proud to focus exclusively on undergraduate education. We place a premium on faculty providing close mentoring through small classrooms and experiential learning. Our students share a passion for learning that goes beyond the classroom across 35 nationally acclaimed and accredited degree programs. A&S students are fueled by a commitment to making a difference in their local and global communities. The College of Arts & Sciences has an impressive record of professional accomplishments by our alumni. Ohio Northern University is ranked #1 in the state of Ohio for Best Value by both the Wall Street Journal and U.S. News & World Report . Located in Ada, Ohio, the University\u2019s rural setting provides a rhythm of life that is peaceful and unhurried. The natural beauty of campus and friendliness of the village and campus communities offer an ideal setting for the pursuit of knowledge and genuine relationships. Additional information about Ohio Northern University is available at http://www.onu.edu . Your next professional chapter begins here! ONU is an equal employment opportunity employer. Accordingly, no person shall be discriminated against on the basis of race, color, sex, gender identity, transgender status, religion, national origin, age, disability, sexual orientation, marital status, military or veteran status, genetic information or any other category protected by federal, state, or local law. This policy applies to all areas of employment including recruitment, hiring, training and development, promotion, transfer, compensation, benefits, discipline, separation and other terms, condition and privileges of employment."}, "https://onu.wd501.myworkdayjobs.com/ONU/job/Ohio-Northern-University/Adjunct-Instructor-of-Mathematics_JR100133": {"title": "Adjunct Instructor of Mathematics", "description": "Posted: 2026-07-29\nPart time\n\nCareer Opportunities at Ohio Northern University Job Summary: The Department of Mathematics & Physics in the Getty College of Arts & Sciences at Ohio Northern University welcomes applicants for a part-time, adjunct faculty position in Mathematics. Candidates with backgrounds in all areas of Mathematics will be considered. We seek a talented individual who is passionate about teaching introductory undergraduate mathematics courses and invested in student success. If you desire to make a difference in the lives of undergraduate students, we invite you to apply. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue in order to fill positions as needed each fall and each spring semester. A master\u2019s degree in Mathematics or 18 hours graduate coursework in Mathematics is required. Candidates with doctoral degrees in Mathematics and experience teaching Mathematics at the university level are encouraged to apply. The successful candidate will demonstrate good interpersonal skills, as well as the interest and ability to mentor students. Please ensure that your CV includes the names and contact information (phone + email) for 3 professional references. Job Description : Successful candidates will serve as instructors of record for introductory mathematics courses or other courses as assigned. Assignments typically consist of one, two, or three courses per semester. Questions concerning the position should be directed to Dr. Jaki Chowdhury, Department Chair of Mathematics & Physics at j-chowdhury@onu.edu. The Getty College of Arts & Sciences is proud to focus exclusively on undergraduate education. We place a premium on faculty providing close mentoring through small classrooms and experiential learning. Our students share a passion for learning that goes beyond the classroom across 35 nationally acclaimed and accredited degree programs. A&S students are fueled by a commitment to making a difference in their local and global communities. The College of Arts & Sciences has an impressive record of professional accomplishments by our alumni. Ohio Northern University is ranked #1 in the state of Ohio for Best Value by both the Wall Street Journal and U.S. News & World Report . Located in Ada, Ohio, the University\u2019s rural setting provides a rhythm of life that is peaceful and unhurried. The natural beauty of campus and friendliness of the village and campus communities offer an ideal setting for the pursuit of knowledge and genuine relationships. Additional information about Ohio Northern University is available at http://www.onu.edu . Your next professional chapter begins here! ONU is an equal employment opportunity employer. Accordingly, no person shall be discriminated against on the basis of race, color, sex, gender identity, transgender status, religion, national origin, age, disability, sexual orientation, marital status, military or veteran status, genetic information or any other category protected by federal, state, or local law. This policy applies to all areas of employment including recruitment, hiring, training and development, promotion, transfer, compensation, benefits, discipline, separation and other terms, condition and privileges of employment."}, "https://onu.wd501.myworkdayjobs.com/ONU/job/Tilton-Hall-Of-Law/Assistant-Professor-of-Law_JR100080": {"title": "Assistant Professor of Law", "description": "Posted: 2026-07-24\nFull time\n\nCareer Opportunities at Ohio Northern University Job Summary: Ohio Northern University's Pettit College of Law seeks candidates for three full-time, entry-level faculty positions on the tenure track. The College of Law has interest in a variety of teaching areas, including but not limited to Contracts, Sales, Secured Transactions, Property, Criminal Law, Criminal Procedure, and Evidence, and qualified lateral candidates will also be considered. ONU Law is a closely knit community focused on preparing practice-ready lawyers, with an Advocacy program ranked among the best in the nation by U.S. News & World Report. Job Description : Ohio Northern University's Pettit College of Law seeks candidates for three full-time, entry-level faculty positions on the tenure track. The College of Law has interest in a variety of teaching areas, including but not limited to Contracts, Sales, Secured Transactions, Property, Criminal Law, Criminal Procedure, and Evidence. Qualified lateral candidates will also be considered. Ohio Northern is a private university affiliated with the United Methodist Church, and its Pettit College of Law is a closely knit community built around small classes and individualized faculty mentoring. For more than 140 years, ONU Law has focused its educational mission on preparing practice-ready lawyers, an emphasis reflected in our clinical and externship placements and an Advocacy program ranked among the best in the nation by U.S. News & World Report. ONU Law is also home to one of the nation's first fully online part-time JD program accredited by the ABA. Candidates with experience as a practicing lawyer, judicial clerk, or law teacher are preferred, and we welcome candidates who bring a range of teaching interests and approaches, including experience with varied instructional formats and delivery methods. Expectations include a normal teaching load of four courses per year, scholarly research and publication, and service obligations for the 2027-2028 academic year. Candidates must have a J.D. from a law school accredited by the A.B.A. or an equivalent degree from a foreign institution, a distinguished academic record, and a commitment to excellence in teaching and scholarship. Ohio Northern University was founded in 1871, and ONU Law has been educating lawyers since 1885. Ohio Northern is located in Ada, Ohio, a quiet college community known for its small-town charm, about an hour from the growing Columbus metro area, and is home to five colleges and about 3,140 students representing 50 states and 15 countries. Ohio Northern University offers a competitive salary package commensurate with the candidate's experience and skills. Fringe benefits include the TIAA-CREF retirement program, medical insurance, disability benefits, life insurance, tuition remission for dependents attending Ohio Northern University for an initial baccalaureate degree, and eligibility for participation in The Tuition Exchange, a program involving over 640 member colleges and universities. Interested candidates are strongly encouraged to apply quickly to ensure immediate review. Interested applicants should send a curriculum vitae, official transcripts from all colleges and educational institutions attended, and the names and contact information of three professional references who have recent knowledge of the applicant's background and potential to Professor Melissa Kidder, Chair, Personnel Committee, at\u00a0 m-kidder@onu.edu , College of Law, Ohio Northern University, 525 S. Main Street, Ada, OH 45810. Equal Opportunity Employer. Interested applicants are encouraged to review the ONU Law website at law.onu.edu. Your next professional chapter begins here! ONU is an equal employment opportunity employer. Accordingly, no person shall be discriminated against on the basis of race, color, sex, gender identity, transgender status, religion, national origin, age, disability, sexual orientation, marital status, military or veteran status, genetic information or any other category protected by federal, state, or local law. This policy applies to all areas of employment including recruitment, hiring, training and development, promotion, transfer, compensation, benefits, discipline, separation and other terms, condition and privileges of employment."}, "https://onu.wd501.myworkdayjobs.com/ONU/job/Ohio-Northern-University/Adjunct-Instructor---College-of-Business_JR100102": {"title": "Adjunct Instructor - College of Business", "description": "Posted: 2026-07-16\nPart time\n\nCareer Opportunities at Ohio Northern University Job Summary: Ohio Northern University welcomes applicants for a part-time, adjunct faculty position. Job Description : We seek an individual passionate about teaching and invested in student success. If you desire to make a difference in the lives of undergraduate students, we invite you to apply for an adjunct faculty position. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue in order to fill positions as needed each semester. Your next professional chapter begins here! ONU is an equal employment opportunity employer. Accordingly, no person shall be discriminated against on the basis of race, color, sex, gender identity, transgender status, religion, national origin, age, disability, sexual orientation, marital status, military or veteran status, genetic information or any other category protected by federal, state, or local law. This policy applies to all areas of employment including recruitment, hiring, training and development, promotion, transfer, compensation, benefits, discipline, separation and other terms, condition and privileges of employment."}, "https://onu.wd501.myworkdayjobs.com/ONU/job/Ohio-Northern-University/Adjunct-Instructor---College-of-Arts---Sciences_JR100098": {"title": "Adjunct Instructor - College of Arts & Sciences", "description": "Posted: 2026-07-16\nPart time\n\nCareer Opportunities at Ohio Northern University Job Summary: Ohio Northern University welcomes applicants for a part-time, adjunct faculty position. Job Description : We seek an individual passionate about teaching and invested in student success. If you desire to make a difference in the lives of undergraduate students, we invite you to apply for an adjunct faculty position. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue in order to fill positions as needed each semester. The Getty College of Arts & Sciences is proud to focus exclusively on undergraduate education. We place a premium on faculty providing close mentoring through small classrooms and experiential learning. Our students share a passion for learning that goes beyond the classroom across 35 nationally acclaimed and accredited degree programs. A&S students are fueled by a commitment to making a difference in their local and global communities. The College of Arts & Sciences has an impressive record of professional accomplishments by our alumni. Ohio Northern University is ranked #1 in the state of Ohio for Best Value by both the Wall Street Journal and U.S. News & World Report . Located in Ada, Ohio, the University\u2019s rural setting provides a rhythm of life that is peaceful and unhurried. The natural beauty of campus and friendliness of the village and campus communities offer an ideal setting for the pursuit of knowledge and genuine relationships. Additional information about Ohio Northern University is available at http://www.onu.edu . A list of academic\u00a0fields of study at Ohio Northern University can be viewed at\u00a0 https://www.onu.edu/academics \u00a0 Your next professional chapter begins here! ONU is an equal employment opportunity employer. Accordingly, no person shall be discriminated against on the basis of race, color, sex, gender identity, transgender status, religion, national origin, age, disability, sexual orientation, marital status, military or veteran status, genetic information or any other category protected by federal, state, or local law. This policy applies to all areas of employment including recruitment, hiring, training and development, promotion, transfer, compensation, benefits, discipline, separation and other terms, condition and privileges of employment."}, "https://onu.wd501.myworkdayjobs.com/ONU/job/Legal-Clinic/Supervising-Attorney_JR100069": {"title": "Supervising Attorney", "description": "Posted: 2026-07-09\nFull time\n\nCareer Opportunities at Ohio Northern University Job Summary: The supervising attorney for the Legal Clinic in Lima works full-time and year-round. As the Lawyers = Justice Coordinator, the supervising attorney mentors and supports a cohort of program Fellows as they establish and develop law practices in surrounding rural Ohio communities. This includes assisting Fellows with practice management, professional development, integration into local legal communities, and collaboration with law students assigned to work with the Fellow on cases. Under the direction of the Director of Legal Clinics, the supervising attorney will also assist in supervising and assessing law students, assisting with case rounds and clinic and externship educational program planning, and participating in orientation, recruitment, trainings, and community events. Job Description : In the role of the Lawyers = Justice Coordinator, the supervising attorney meets regularly with program Fellows to provide mentorship, case consultation, and professional guidance; assists Fellows in establishing and operating solo or small law practices; facilitates collaboration between Fellows and law students working on Fellow cases; and helps Fellows integrate into local bar associations, courts, and community organizations. The supervising attorney also assists with case coverage during Fellow to help ensure continuity of client representation.\u00a0 Under the direction of the Director of Legal Clinics, the supervising attorney will also supervise clinic students, support case strategy discussions, and assist with case coverage, including serving as attorney of record as assigned.\u00a0 Vacations should be scheduled around the requirement of maintaining effective case coverage. Some evening and occasional weekend hours will be expected. The supervising attorney works under the supervision of the Director of Legal Clinics and may be assigned additional responsibilities by the Director. Your next professional chapter begins here! ONU is an equal employment opportunity employer. Accordingly, no person shall be discriminated against on the basis of race, color, sex, gender identity, transgender status, religion, national origin, age, disability, sexual orientation, marital status, military or veteran status, genetic information or any other category protected by federal, state, or local law. This policy applies to all areas of employment including recruitment, hiring, training and development, promotion, transfer, compensation, benefits, discipline, separation and other terms, condition and privileges of employment."}, "https://onu.wd501.myworkdayjobs.com/ONU/job/Ohio-Northern-University/Assistant-Coach-of-Football--Part-Time-_JR100066": {"title": "Assistant Coach of Football (Part-Time)", "description": "Posted: 2026-07-07\nPart time\n\nCareer Opportunities at Ohio Northern University Job Summary: The part-time coach will be responsible for coaching a position group as well as having their own recruiting area. This position will work with all aspects of a college football program. Job Description : Primary responsibilites include but are not limited to: Coaching a position group Recruiting own area Practice and game film coordination Required Skills: Computer literacy Organization Good communication skills Strong work ethic Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor's Degree Your next professional chapter begins here! ONU is an equal employment opportunity employer. Accordingly, no person shall be discriminated against on the basis of race, color, sex, gender identity, transgender status, religion, national origin, age, disability, sexual orientation, marital status, military or veteran status, genetic information or any other category protected by federal, state, or local law. This policy applies to all areas of employment including recruitment, hiring, training and development, promotion, transfer, compensation, benefits, discipline, separation and other terms, condition and privileges of employment."}, "https://onu.wd501.myworkdayjobs.com/ONU/job/Ohio-Northern-University/Adjunct-Instructor---College-of-Engineering_JR100005": {"title": "Adjunct Instructor - College of Engineering", "description": "Posted: 2026-06-15\nPart time\n\nCareer Opportunities at Ohio Northern University Job Summary: Ohio Northern University welcomes applicants for a part-time, adjunct faculty position. Job Description : We seek an individual passionate about teaching and invested in student success. If you desire to make a difference in the lives of undergraduate students, we invite you to apply for an adjunct faculty position. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue in order to fill positions as needed each semester. A list of academic\u00a0fields of study at Ohio Northern University can be viewed at\u00a0 https://www.onu.edu/academics \u00a0 Your next professional chapter begins here! ONU is an equal employment opportunity employer. Accordingly, no person shall be discriminated against on the basis of race, color, sex, gender identity, transgender status, religion, national origin, age, disability, sexual orientation, marital status, military or veteran status, genetic information or any other category protected by federal, state, or local law. This policy applies to all areas of employment including recruitment, hiring, training and development, promotion, transfer, compensation, benefits, discipline, separation and other terms, condition and privileges of employment."}, "https://onu.wd501.myworkdayjobs.com/ONU/job/Ohio-Northern-University/Assistant-Director-of-Student-Involvement-and-Coordinator-of-Fraternity---Sorority-Life_JR100328": {"title": "Assistant Director of Student Involvement and Coordinator of Fraternity & Sorority Life", "description": "Posted: 2026-10-21\nFull time\n\nCareer Opportunities at Ohio Northern University Job Summary: The Assistant Director of Student Involvement & Coordinator of Fraternity & Sorority Life advises fraternity and sorority organizations, supports student leaders, and oversees all campus student groups and the engagement platform. Job Description : The Assistant Director of Student Involvement & Coordinator of Fraternity & Sorority Life serves as the primary contact and advisor for fraternities and sororities (FSL), student leaders, alumni, and inter/national organizations. The Assistant Director oversees all student organizations including the creation and maintenance of groups as well as the campus engagement platform. Primary Responsibilities Oversee fraternity and sorority life on campus including the oversight of chapters,\u00a0 councils and honorary organizations as well as the communication and regular correspondence with chapter presidents and leaders, advisors, housing and alumni boards, and national offices. Lead and support FSL community programming initiatives including the annual Standards of Excellence Program as a means of evaluation and recognition of FSL chapters. Maintain policies and records for FSL pertaining to recruitment, academics, membership and conduct. Manage the campus engagement platform including but not limited to the process for creating new organizations, maintenance of organizations and all campus events. Serve as a point of contact for campus events including safety plans, liability waivers, and appropriate risk management procedures. Assist with major campus events and programs including but not limited to Ada Community Engagement Day, International Polar Bear Day and President\u2019s Leadership Dessert. Manage and update the FSL website in addition to overseeing marketing initiatives via social media for FSL and Student Life. Assist with student body communication via monitoring of the student-l and oversight of the Polar Bear Post. Perform other duties as assigned. Minimum Qualifications Ability to work evenings and weekends as needed. Bachelor\u2019s degree in Student Personnel Services, Higher Education or a closely related area. Two years of experience in FSL, Student Affairs, or student programming as a professional/paraprofessional. Preferred Qualifications Master\u2019s degree in Student Personnel Services, Higher Education or a closely related area. Your next professional chapter begins here! ONU is an equal employment opportunity employer. Accordingly, no person shall be discriminated against on the basis of race, color, sex, gender identity, transgender status, religion, national origin, age, disability, sexual orientation, marital status, military or veteran status, genetic information or any other category protected by federal, state, or local law. This policy applies to all areas of employment including recruitment, hiring, training and development, promotion, transfer, compensation, benefits, discipline, separation and other terms, condition and privileges of employment."}}, "rows": {"https://onu.wd501.myworkdayjobs.com/ONU/job/Ohio-Northern-University/Adjunct-Instructor-of-Pharmacy_JR100323": {"school_id": 1019, "posting_url": "https://onu.wd501.myworkdayjobs.com/ONU/job/Ohio-Northern-University/Adjunct-Instructor-of-Pharmacy_JR100323", "job_title_in_post": "Adjunct Instructor of Pharmacy", "position_type": "Lecturer", "job_term": "Part-time", "department_or_school": "College of 